# Render pipeline — quality floor

Before **any** optimization to plates, bake, clean, or encode, read **`pipeline.md`** and this floor.

## Do not soften

- **`QUALITY_ID`** `wt-q2` in `encode.mjs`; **`assertX264Args`**, **`plateJpegQ()`** throw if softer.
- Recorder/clean: x264 **ultrafast -qp 0** (lossless intermediates).
- Plates: **veryfast CRF 4**, JPEG **q95**, 1920×1080, **BT.709** via `toBt709()` (Chromium JPEG is BT.601 — green if untagged).
- Delivery: **medium CRF 12**; variant CRF 16 — **no VideoToolbox** shortcut that changes quality model.
- **Version snapshots** are user-facing — prefer APFS **clone** (`COPYFILE_FICLONE`) over deleting history.

## Log shape (UI parses these)

Keep progress lines stable, e.g.:

- `» plate · <label> · frame N of M`
- `» plates · …`
- `» live · N%`
- `» encode · N%`
- `» cards · Bake …`

## Safe optimization targets (examples from issue #26 work)

- Plate cache keys: **htmlHash + cssHash + pipeline + qc**, not naive mtime-only.
- Reduce redundant **double rAF** only with **PSNR ≥ 60 dB** vs golden frames.
- Bake: prefer **Metal** on darwin where documented; overlay graph **x/y** for cropped captions.
- **`validate.mjs`**: output-side **`-ss` after `-i`** for QC grabs — changing order breaks byte-identical grabs.

## Studio Render button path

`decideAction` → optional **record** → plates → produce (plates again, bakes, clean, encode) → audio → deliver → version snapshot. **Quick render** skips capture; pace/camera changes may still need **re-record** for take truth.

## When user asks for speed

1. Measure on fixture slug **`walkthrough-studio`** (or named project).
2. Document in issue/PR: wall time, plate ms/frame, bake, encode.
3. Run **`node --test kit/lib/*.test.mjs`** + real produce smoke if touching encode/plates/bake.
